{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple","id":1363787,"title":"Simplified Grapple","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-28T07:27:26-08:00","id":1363787,"title":"Simplified Grapple","content":"So I know Lioness gave ideas around here to simplify Grapple to have it be less of rolling 5 times because it's annoying.<br /> <br /> I don't remember the specific ideas, but most are certainly to her credits, at the moment, I'm thinking something like this could work, keep the spirit of grapple present, and obviously make some Charms useless (but do I care about Charms about a mechanic that is poorly usable ? I don't think so).<br /> <br /> 1) Make a Gambit attack against (enemy Strength) goal number on damage (2 rolls : 1 to hit, 1 to roll damage)<br /> 2) You get your number of control turns by the threshold of which you surpassed the difficulty of the gambit (+your own strength, I'm not decided about that yet) (0 rolls)<br /> 3) You gain (Your Strength) initiative, which emulates a Savage Withering attack on the enemy, and factor your strength into your overall action (0 roll)<br /> <br /> End of your turn on the gambit Grapple. You cannot take another &quot;special grapple&quot; action on this turn.<br /> <br /> Your following turns work exactly the same as described in the book.<br /> <br /> My short analysis : I guess it can be considered some sort of nerf on the efficacy of Grapple because it locks potential 1 turn lock someone and throw them with Charms bonus and stuff, but I don't see how it is possible to reduce the amount of rolls on this Grapple thing and at the same time keep the same balance. If it has to go through nerfing a 5 rolls boring mechanical mini-game I'm fine with it. I'm open to suggestions and remarks, still.<br /> <br /> Old amount of roll on a Grapple (worst and to my experience usual case) : 5<br /> New amount of rolls on a Grapple : 2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T09:01:38-08:00","id":1363793,"title":"","content":"Do you think a grappler should suffer a penalty to any attempt to avoid a counter-grapple from the opponent they are clinching?<br /> <br /> I definitely want the system to encourage two grapplers to clinch each other at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T09:03:16-08:00","id":1363794,"title":"","content":"That... makes hella sense. Way easier than what we have currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T09:26:38-08:00","id":1363797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple#post1363787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My short analysis : I guess it can be considered some sort of nerf on the efficacy of Grapple because it locks potential 1 turn lock someone and throw them with Charms bonus and stuff, but I don't see how it is possible to reduce the amount of rolls on this Grapple thing and at the same time keep the same balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Option 1: Relegate &quot;throw someone in the same action as you grabbed them&quot; to Charms. Solar Brawl and Mantis Style can easily gain at least one more Charm each for that.<br /> <br /> Option 2: Create TWO different grapple gambits.<br /> <br /> The first one works like your model here. The second one is an immediate slam/throw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T09:32:07-08:00","id":1363799,"title":"","content":"If you want to preserve the first turn action, you could remove the gambit roll to make room for a damage roll :<br /> <br /> 1) make a decisive attack roll.<br /> 2) threshold successes become rounds of control<br /> 3) subtract the gambit cost, gambit is automatically successful<br /> 4) the free attack automatically succeeds and has the same number of threshold successes as the grapple attack roll<br /> 5) roll damage normally<br /> <br /> That way you still only have 2 rolls to make (steps 1 and 5).<br /> <br /> As another alternative, Lumi's Hissatsu (on the Exalted Discord) also reduces Grapples to 2 rolls (Attack Roll + Control Roll), but the Grapple rework is part of a broader combat rework and can't really be used on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 01-28-2020, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T10:13:26-08:00","id":1363804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1363793#post1363793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a grappler should suffer a penalty to any attempt to avoid a counter-grapple from the opponent they are clinching?<br /> <br /> I definitely want the system to encourage two grapplers to clinch each other at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I do not master English enough to understand exactly what you are saying. Could you expand a bit more ?<br /> <br /> To answer your other post :<br /> <br /> 1) Thing is I want to get rid of too many rolls for this specific action, not gatekeep it behind a Charm. HOWEVER, I think you said something very interesting that I didn't think of before : Look at the Charm Heaven Thunder Hammer. It effectively gives the same mechanical effect as a Throw/slam action, ie : throw someone away, and deals damage depending on the range. The main difference lies in the notion of Control Round that only exist in Grapple Gambits, but as was said by Epitome later, the Control round could be calculated on the spot as the threshold success to hit. Throw/slam would disappear as a &quot;core Grapple move&quot;, and become available in this way in the form of a Charm that is a decisive attack, resembling Heaven Thunder Hammer essentially, and each Exalt type could personnalize it. <br /> <br /> 2) I think what I just proposed earlier kinda answer this proposition, since I would effectively eliminate the &quot;Throw/slam&quot; option and create a Charm that acts like this.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> Actually your option is interesting. I'll consider it and try to come with an answer soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T02:31:48-08:00","id":1363936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1363799#post1363799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to preserve the first turn action, you could remove the gambit roll to make room for a damage roll :<br /> <br /> 1) make a decisive attack roll.<br /> 2) threshold successes become rounds of control<br /> 3) subtract the gambit cost, gambit is automatically successful<br /> 4) the free attack automatically succeeds and has the same number of threshold successes as the grapple attack roll<br /> 5) roll damage normally<br /> <br /> That way you still only have 2 rolls to make (steps 1 and 5).</div> </div> </div> </div>After reflexion, I'm not sure to be interested by that.<br /> <br /> My reasoning is the following : Usually when someone wants to grapple, what they want is either to Hold the opponent, wither them and prevent them from moving, or throw them for maximum damage.<br /> <br /> The throw for maximum damage is kind of annoying because this is really a mini-game inside the mini-game to represent some sort of special kind of interaction with the Grapple decisive attack, but it actually offers no other real value than being the same thing as Heaven Thunder Hammer but different. While I feel your solution &quot;work mechanically&quot;, if what the player wants is to directly damage the opponent, I'd call for a normal decisive attack. <br /> <br /> The Hold could actually be interesting, and I guess making it possible to Hold on first turn after gaining the Grapple instead of gaining initiative is good.<br /> <br /> Doing a withering is annoying because we have to go all the way making a new attack when we basically just resolved one, hence my suggestion to give automatic initiative depending on the Grappler's strength.<br /> <br /> So my intent is to allow most actions that would not be already emulated by directly making a normal decisive attack with some particularities (essentially Throw/Slam). To keep the core of Grappling that you are physically engaged with the opponent (Allowing Hold and Withering), but reduce the number rolls for this (essentially resolve automatically the Withering, because we had enough roll at that point).<br /> <br /> I get that the Grappling system intends to emulate a special kind of interaction that is restraining enemies, I just happen to think that in a game with 1000 Charms, wanting to hold on the specific subsystem that takes too much time to resolve while it could be represented narratively the same way, and with fewer rolls should be preferred. I think there won't be overall agreement on the way to do that, but I wanted to present a simpler way to do it. I don't think Epitome's proposition its better or worse, just that you have to chose one for how to handle this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T11:38:10-08:00","id":1363998,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest the difficulty should be higher of their Strength or Brawl though (or maybe even Dex, if they're wriggling away).<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest that I think it'd make more sense if the enemy lost higher of your Strength or Brawl initiative, rather than you gaining it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old amount of roll on a Grapple (worst and to my experience usual case) : 5 </div> </div> </div>Bears do 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T12:27:17-08:00","id":1364004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1363998#post1363998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest the difficulty should be higher of their Strength or Brawl though (or maybe even Dex, if they're wriggling away).<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest that I think it'd make more sense if the enemy lost higher of your Strength or Brawl initiative, rather than you gaining it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second, I think, is a very good idea-- it keeps the essence of the turn-one savage attack, but doesn't instantly refill the Ini you just spent on the Gambit.<br /> <br /> The former...I'm not sure about. On the one hand, it makes a lot of sense, and helps keep Grapple from being inescapably overwhelming for non-Str/Brawl characters. On the other, Dexterity is already pretty damn dominant, and &quot;dodging out of the way&quot; is already represented by the initial attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T13:14:38-08:00","id":1364011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1363998#post1363998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest the difficulty should be higher of their Strength or Brawl though (or maybe even Dex, if they're wriggling away).<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest that I think it'd make more sense if the enemy lost higher of your Strength or Brawl initiative, rather than you gaining it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bears do 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually hesitating. I think you might be right though, concerning your second proposition. I'll keep it, I think it's a good idea.<br /> <br /> Like Grod though, I'm not sure about the Dexterity part on your first one (I think higher of Strength or Brawl is fine), as said Dexterity is prominent and I'd like not to increase its overall utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T13:21:42-08:00","id":1364014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1364004#post1364004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;dodging out of the way&quot; is already represented by the initial attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good point. Higher of Str/Brawl then.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that this is going to really put a crimper on initiative though. It's going to cost you 4-6 initiative to do the grapple most of the time, knock of 3-5 of their initiative... everyone's going to be down initiative. Which... maybe makes sense for a grapple?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T13:41:48-08:00","id":1364024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1364014#post1364014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that this is going to really put a crimper on initiative though. It's going to cost you 4-6 initiative to do the grapple most of the time, knock of 3-5 of their initiative... everyone's going to be down initiative. Which... maybe makes sense for a grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. A gambit is giving up momentum to hinder your enemy, and getting caught in a chokehold certainly ought to screw with your combat flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T23:29:16-08:00","id":1364107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363787-simplified-grapple?p=1364014#post1364014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, good point. Higher of Str/Brawl then.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that this is going to really put a crimper on initiative though. It's going to cost you 4-6 initiative to do the grapple most of the time, knock of 3-5 of their initiative... everyone's going to be down initiative. Which... maybe makes sense for a grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just woke up thinking this and wanting to post it here but you apparently got my back.<br /> <br /> I think ot requires a bit of test. I prefer when the fight always moving forward, so everyone losing initiative is not really my jam, but a bit of playtest should help to figure it out","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}